# Build context for the Dockerfile. The build reads package*.json,
# index.html, vite.config.ts, tsconfig*.json, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, public/, src/ and backend/;
# scripts/ stays in the context for build steps. Everything below is never
# needed (and some of it should never reach the build daemon).

# VCS, editors, agents
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store

# Dependencies and build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
dist
bin
build
backend/kubebench
backend/internal/web/dist

# Local state and credentials
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
.env
.env.*
kubeconfig*

# Repository content that is not part of the image
charts
deploy
packaging
docs
examples
*.md
# ...except the changelog, which the frontend bundles for What's new.
!CHANGELOG.md
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
install.sh
Makefile
.goreleaser.yaml
backend/**/*_test.go
backend/**/testdata
